From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer window: retry a failed allocation without HW_FB

On the SM-T113 (Spreadtrum SC7730S) the gralloc HAL backs buffers that carry
GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB with a 5 MiB carveout heap, and the composer HAL already
fills it with its own two 1024x600 RGBA framebuffer targets. The window's own
buffers (usage x1e02, set by libGLES_mali.so) then fail with EIO.

Retry once without the framebuffer bit, so the buffer can come from the
regular heap, and print both results.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [SC7730S-specific workaround; a proper fix is to size the carveout]
---
--- a/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
+++ b/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,19 @@
         fprintf(stderr, "hybris-hwcomposer: gralloc allocate %ux%u format x%x usage x%" PRIx64 " failed: %d (%s)\n",
                 width, height, format, usage, status, strerror(status < 0 ? -status : status));
         handle = NULL;
+
+        // Some gralloc implementations back GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB buffers with a small dedicated
+        // carveout (5 MiB on the SC7730S, which the composer HAL already fills with its own two
+        // framebuffer targets). Try again without the framebuffer bit before giving up.
+        if (usage & GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB) {
+            uint64_t retry = usage & ~(uint64_t)GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB;
+            stride = 0;
+            status = hybris_gralloc_allocate(width, height, format, (uint32_t)retry, &handle, (uint32_t*)&stride);
+            fprintf(stderr, "hybris-hwcomposer: retry without HW_FB, usage x%" PRIx64 ": %d (%s)\n",
+                    retry, status, strerror(status < 0 ? -status : status));
+            if (status)
+                handle = NULL;
+        }
     }
 
     TRACE("width=%d height=%d stride=%d format=x%x usage=x%" PRIx64 "status=%s this=%p",
